Visual Prompt Studio 1.2
Prompt: Create an Acoustic Folk album cover that depicts a group of friends running down a hiking trail with lots of greenery. The album cover should invoke feelings of living in the present with friends. Make the album cover look lightly blurred with a focus point on the trail that is ahead of the group. Emphasize the quiet nature with soft even lighting coming from the top left side of the album cover. Add details to the swirls and leaves on the trees around them. The group depicted in the cover should outweigh the symetrical balance of the whole picture. Include a green and orange color pallete with hues of dark blue for depth emphasis.
Vocabulary Breakdown: Value - often considered more important than color in a piece of artwork because it creates contrast and depth. Space - this can either be physical space in a piece of art or within the painting. Can also be negative and positive space, often leading the viewer to either a main focus of the art piece or the surroundings of a subject. Unity - can be multiple subjects bringing in the artwork or creating the artwork itself. Balance - creates symmetry or accentuates the asymmetry in a piece. Can also apply to color. Rhythm - Like music, this creates the feeling of accelerated flow or steady, etc. Often can be called a visual tempo.
